body:
While looking to correct this bug, I saw this comment on the RefinementList connector:

// Setting the value to an empty string ensures that it is persisted in
// the URL as an empty value.
// This is necessary in the case where `defaultRefinement` contains one
// item and we try to deselect it. `nextSelected` would be an empty array,
// which would not be persisted to the URL.
// {foo: \['bar']} => "foo\[0]=bar"
// {foo: \[]} => ""

@vvo @Morhaus : do you remember the reason for that choice to persist empty value in the URL?
